  "narrative": "All estimates below are signed to the registered hypothesis direction. H137 and H247 directly localize the PTEN-loss STAT3 effect within interferon strata. In high-IFN contexts, PTEN loss is associated with much stronger STAT3 dependency (H137: +0.324 [0.249, 0.399]); in low-IFN contexts the association remains strong but smaller (H247: +0.208 [0.136, 0.280]). The approximate difference between strata agrees with H241 and supports the accepted but borderline interferon modification, although the lower bound of the original interaction is small and this remains exploratory dataset-specific evidence. H250 extends the high-IFN PTEN effect into adherent culture (+0.290 [0.204, 0.377]), making the interaction less likely to be an artifact of a small non-adherent subset, but I keep H241 active and register an adherent-only interaction to test whether the interferon difference itself persists after restricting to adherent lines. H248 and H252 give the expected positive contrast for NF1 loss among KRAS-WT lines: less negative KRAS dependency, i.e. weaker dependency. H248 KRAS-WT adherent gives +0.048 [0.011, 0.084], and H252 KRAS-WT/BRAF-WT adherent gives +0.046 [0.009, 0.083]. These point estimates are meaningfully larger than the 10% scale criterion relative to KRAS dependency baselines, but lower bounds are small and the effect is secondary; I accept them as dataset-specific associations with residual uncertainty and no causal interpretation. I keep them active to assess culture-context heterogeneity, not to re-open the original main effects. H249 and H253 are strong direct confirmations of TP53-loss weaker USP7 dependency in adenocarcinoma (+0.385 [0.299, 0.471]) and high-serum context (+0.443 [0.353, 0.532]); I accept and close them. H254-H256 are strong direct confirmations of KEAP1-loss weaker NFE2L2 dependency in adenocarcinoma TP53-loss lines and in both interferon strata (approximately +0.78 to +0.81, all intervals excluding zero); these robustly localize the accepted KEAP1 axis and are accepted and closed. H140 and H257 are strong direct confirmations of MSI-high stronger WRN dependency in high- and low-IFN contexts (approximately +0.79, intervals excluding zero); these support stability of the MSI-high axis across immune-signature contexts and are accepted and closed. No validation request is made because the voluntary validation budget is exhausted. The main caution is multiplicity: the PTEN-loss/STAT3 interferon interaction is supported by complementary strata but remains borderline and unvalidated, so it should be treated as dataset-specific localization rather than proof of a general biological modifier.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 14 appraise update. Validation budget is exhausted. Newly delivered results are discovery associations only. PTEN-loss STAT3 dependency is now strongly supported within high IFN (H137, R170: +0.324 [0.249, 0.399]) and low IFN (H247, R171: +0.208 [0.136, 0.280]), with H250 showing high-IFN adherent lines also show strong effect (R172: +0.290 [0.204, 0.377]). The high-stratum estimate exceeds the low-stratum estimate by about 0.116, consistent with accepted borderline interaction H241. Treat H241 as active but dataset-specific; test adherent-only IFN interaction and low-IFN adherent main effect next. NF1-loss among KRAS-WT lines is associated with weaker KRAS dependency: accepted H111/H123 are now supported in adherent contexts, H248 (R173: +0.048 [0.011, 0.084]) and H252 (R174: +0.046 [0.009, 0.083]). Accept H248/H252 as secondary dataset-specific effects with cautious uncertainty; test culture interaction but do not overinterpret lineage/culture differences. TP53-loss USP7 association remains very strong and stable in adenocarcinoma (H249) and high serum (H253). KEAP1-loss NFE2L2 association remains very strong and stable in adenocarcinoma TP53-loss (H254), high IFN (H255), and low IFN (H256). MSI-high WRN association remains very strong and stable in high IFN (H140) and low IFN (H257). Core accepted axes remain: SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 stronger dependency, MSI-high/WRN stronger dependency, KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 weaker dependency, CDKN2A-loss/MDM2 stronger dependency, TP53-loss/USP7 weaker dependency, PTEN-loss/STAT3 stronger dependency, and secondary NF1-loss/KRAS-WT weaker KRAS dependency. Negative or unsupported areas remain large: direct KRAS/BRAF/EGFR/ERBB2 driver associations, MYC amplification/high-MYC dependency axes, RB1-loss/KIF18A, constructed markers D/E/F, and many context interactions. Do not treat invalid underpowered co-loss cells as evidence of absence. All conclusions are associations in this supplied dataset, not causal or generalizable claims.",
